---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const repo = 'https://github.com/dragid10/which-filament';
---

<Base title="Contribute" description="Add or correct a filament entry: it's just a Markdown file.">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <section class="page-head"><div>
      <h1>Help improve which-filament</h1>
      <p class="lede">Every filament on this site is a single Markdown file. Fixing or adding one takes a few minutes.</p>
    </div></section>
    <h2>Spotted something wrong?</h2>
    <p>Open a <a href={`${repo}/issues/new/choose`}>"Correct information"</a> issue, or use the "Suggest an edit" link at the bottom of any filament page to edit the file directly on GitHub.</p>
    <h2>Want a new filament type added?</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Open an <a href={`${repo}/issues/new/choose`}>"Add a filament"</a> issue, or</li>
      <li>Copy an existing file in <code>src/content/filaments/</code>, edit it, and open a pull request.</li>
    </ol>
    <h2>Want to add an example object?</h2>
    <p>Copy a file in <code>src/content/objects/</code>, name the best filament, and explain why. Filament names are checked by the build, so typos can't slip through.</p>
    <p>The build checks the frontmatter automatically and tells you exactly what's missing or invalid. Full instructions are in <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>CONTRIBUTING.md</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
